      "sc:author": "Satish Kamatkar",
      "sc:description": "Open-source implementation of the 2024 Animal Variant Classification Guidelines (AVCG). Given the evidence for a genetic variant in an animal, it applies the guideline's 23 evidence criteria and its decision rules, and gives one of five classifications: pathogenic, likely pathogenic, uncertain significance, likely benign or benign. Every result shows which criteria were met and which rule decided the label. Runs from the command line, one variant or a batch, with text, JSON and report output.",
      "sc:featureList": {
        "@id": "edam:operation_3225"
      },
